## Backend coupling

- `getMasterData` → `TLCG_CORE_BACKEND` — employees, Goods-KTT, suppliers (shared with all workflows)
- `purchaseRequest` → `TLCG_P2P_BACKEND` — writes to `Purchase_Request_History` sheet; sends emails to requester + budget + supplier approvers only
- `getPurchaseRequestHistory` → `TLCG_P2P_BACKEND` — returns slim `requests[]` (no line items, no metadata JSON). `getPurchaseRequest` loads one purchase when the drawer opens. `searchPurchaseRequests` looks up the archive.
- `approvePurchaseRequest` → `TLCG_P2P_BACKEND` — updates `metadata.{role}Status`, computes next status via `computePRApprovalState_`, emails the purchasing approver only when that stage opens
- `rejectPurchaseRequest` → `TLCG_P2P_BACKEND` — sets status=`Đã từ chối`, writes `metadata.rejectionNote`; gated so only the active stage's approver can reject

**`BACKEND_URL = '/api/voucher'`** — do NOT hardcode a direct GAS exec URL. The proxy runs on Ubuntu (`api/voucher.js`), not Vercel.

