## Submit payload (`purchaseRequest`)

**Encoding:** Always send as `data=<JSON>` field (NOT flat URL-encoded params):
```js
const sendParams = new URLSearchParams();
sendParams.append('data', JSON.stringify(payload));
```
This matches the voucher.html pattern and reliably flows through the Vercel proxy → GAS `params.data → JSON.parse(params.data)`.

Fields in the JSON payload:
```text
action, prNo, companyCode, companyName, department, requesterName, requesterEmail,
requiredDate, priority, currency, items (JSON string of line objects),
grandTotal, purpose,
vendorName, vendorType, vendorTaxId, vendorAddress,
vendorAccountName, vendorAccountNo, vendorBankName, vendorTransferNote,
budgetCode,
budgetApprover (required), budgetApproverNote,
supplierApprover (required), supplierApproverNote,
contractApprover (optional), purchasingApprover (optional),
submittedAt,
requesterSignature (base64), attachments (JSON string of [{fileName, fileData, mimeType}])
```

**Metadata JSON** (col Q) initialized at submit to include per-role status:
```json
{
  "budgetStatus": "Pending",
  "supplierStatus": "Pending",
  "contractStatus": "Pending | N/A",
  "purchasingStatus": "Pending | N/A",
  "requesterEmail": "...",
  "budgetApproverNote": "...",
  "supplierApproverNote": "...",
  ...
}
```
Roles not assigned at submit get `N/A` status (auto-skipped by `computePRApprovalState_`).

## Items line object structure

Each row in `items` JSON array uses:
```js
{ section, loai, desc, qty, unit, price, total, note }
```
**Key field is `desc`** (from `.item-desc` input) — NOT `name` or `itemName`.

When rendering items in the drawer or print view, always check `item.desc` first:
```js
item.desc || item.name || item.itemName || '—'
```

## Attachments (supporting documents)

- Collected as `File` objects in `_attachmentFiles[]`
- At submit time, converted to base64 via `_fileToBase64()` and sent as `attachments` JSON string inside the `data` field
- GAS backend (`handlePurchaseRequest`) uploads to Drive via `DriveApp` using folder ID from `getCfg_('PURCHASE_REQUEST_FOLDER_ID', '1SJ-pUa6jg2rmJTzle-TvvSNrKMUduvx3')`
- Drive URLs stored in `metadata.attachments[]` as `{fileName, fileUrl}`
- **Never use `/api/drive-upload`** (no Service Account quota on personal Drive)

## Approval workflow (Phase 3 — Phê Duyệt)

Implements the global P2P approval model:

```
Submit → Parallel: Budget + Supplier
       → Purchasing, only if assigned
       → Hoàn thành
Full branch contract review happens in contract.html, not in this PR approve chain.
```

### `computePRApprovalState_(row, metadata)` in `TLCG_P2P_BACKEND.gs`

Central helper used by approve, reject, and submit to determine:
- Active `stage`: `'parallel'` | `'contract'` | `'purchasing'` | `'complete'`
- `statusLabel` (written to col O)
- Email addresses for each role

**Stage advancement rules:**
- `parallel` active while any of `{budget, supplier}` is assigned but not `Approved`
- In-PR `contract` stage does not open: `skipPRContract` is true for `full` and `simplified`
- `purchasing` opens only when parallel is complete AND a purchasing email is assigned
- Unassigned optional roles are auto-skipped (`N/A` initial status)

### Status labels in sheet (col O)

| Stage | Status text |
|-------|-------------|
| After submit | `Đang duyệt ngân sách & NCC (2/5)` |
| Contract active | `Thẩm định Hợp đồng (4/5)` |
| Purchasing active | `Mua hàng (5/5)` |
| Done | `Hoàn thành` |
| Rejected | `Đã từ chối` |

### Frontend stage helper

`_computePRStage(pr, meta)` in `purchase_request.html` mirrors the backend and returns `{ stage, budgetEmail, supplierEmail, contractEmail, purchasingEmail }`. Used by `_isMyPRTask` and drawer action gating.

### Gate checks (BE + FE)

- Approver may only act when their role's stage is the currently active one
- Budget approving does NOT advance status until Supplier also approves (parallel stays open)
- Out-of-order approve attempts are rejected with clear message

