## When editing this flow

- `BACKEND_URL` in `purchase_request.html` must stay as **`/api/voucher`** — never hardcode a direct GAS exec URL.
- To rotate the P2P deployment URL, update `TLCG_P2P_BACKEND_URL` in the Ubuntu app env, then restart `tlcg-workflow`.
- After a successful send, `resetForm()` must re-enable `#submit-btn`. Leaving it disabled blocks the next request until a full reload.
- Align **`Goods-KTT`** sheet headers with `seedGoods` column names (`Items`, `Min. Order`, `Status`, `Category`, `Unit`, `Specification`, `CUKCUK/QBO Code`).
- `Purchase_Request_History` sheet is auto-created on first submit if missing.
- If the browser number is already used, the server assigns the next free number and returns it as `prNo`. Show that returned number. Approval, rejection, and send-back send `submittedAt` with the number so a shared number still updates the submission that was opened. Splitting two different purchases that already share a number is `runPurchaseRequestMaintenance` in the Apps Script editor, once. It is not part of opening the list.
- The list reads open purchases plus the latest 5,000 rows, and returns a short card. Line items and metadata load with `getPurchaseRequest` when the drawer opens. New purchase-request actions are written to `PR_Audit_Log` only. A finished purchase with no activity for 90 days moves to `Purchase_Request_Archive` at most once a day. Open approvals stay on `Purchase_Request_History`.
- `computePRApprovalState_` is the single source of truth for active stage in GAS. `_computePRStage` in `purchase_request.html` mirrors it client-side. Keep them in sync if logic changes.
